---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie policy — Freighthub"
  description="Freighthub sets no cookies of its own and runs no analytics or advertising scripts. What the hosting provider may set, and how to control cookies in your browser."
>
  <article>
    <h1>Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="article-meta">Last reviewed 15 November 2026</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Freighthub is a static site with no login, no forms and no analytics. It does not set cookies for
      measurement, advertising or personalisation.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies set by this site</h2>
    <p>
      None. There is no analytics script, no advertising tag, no embedded video, no comment system and
      no A/B testing tool. Reading a page does not create a profile.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies a provider may set</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Set by</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Type</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>__cf_bm</code> and similar</td>
          <td>The CDN and hosting provider</td>
          <td>Distinguish browsers from automated traffic and keep the service available</td>
          <td>Essential, short-lived</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      This cookie is set by the infrastructure that serves the site, not by Freighthub's own code, and
      it is not used to build an advertising profile. If the hosting provider changes its cookie set,
      this table is updated.
    </p>

    <h2>Email links</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages contain <code>mailto:</code> links. Clicking one opens your mail client; it does not
      set a cookie on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking the provider's security cookie
      may cause automated checks to treat your browser as a bot, but it will not prevent you reading
      the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a> — what is processed and why. <a href="/terms/">Terms of
      use</a> — the basis on which the site is published.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
